      "body": "## Motivation\n\nThe direct-linker pool groups pack draft depth N onto the transfer layer of target layer N (DSA with MTP/EAGLE/DSpark draft pools, DeepSeek-V4 paged SWA with a draft), so one logical layer maps to several device buffers. UMBP's layer ordering treated the tuple as a broken bijection and refused to start.\n\nSplit out of #44623 per review.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Walk every buffer index of a mapped layer when ordering UMBP pool layers, rejecting a buffer mapped twice.\n- Emit every buffer of a packed layer in one UMBP range group.\n- Unit test for the packed target/draft ranges.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Unit test passes.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #39067700265](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39067700265)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #39067700304](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39067700304)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #39067700231](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/39067700231)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
